### Mini LMS REST API Testing File (VS Code REST Client compatible)
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@token = {{loginStudent.response.body.token}}
@instructorToken = {{loginInstructor.response.body.token}}

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1

### 2. Register New Student
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice.student@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "student"
}

### 3. Register New Instructor
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Dr. Alan Turing",
  "email": "alan.instructor@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "instructor"
}

### 4. Login Student (Extracts Bearer Token)
# @name loginStudent
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice.student@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 5. Login Instructor (Extracts Instructor Bearer Token)
# @name loginInstructor
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alan.instructor@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6. Get Current User Profile (Protected - Bearer Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get All Published Courses (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses HTTP/1.1

### 8. Search Courses by Keyword & Category
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?search=Web&category=Programming HTTP/1.1

### 9. Create Course (Instructor Only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{instructorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Full-Stack Web Development with Node.js & PostgreSQL",
  "description": "Master modern full-stack development covering Express, PostgreSQL, REST APIs, and responsive design.",
  "category": "Web Development",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1593720213428-28a5b9e94613?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&q=80"
}
